Key decisions for IPQ8074 specifically:

KASAN is disabled — it requires 8x memory overhead and the IPQ8074 has 512MB-1GB. It would cause OOM crashes. Everything else is safe for this platform.

SHADOW_CALL_STACK is aarch64-specific — uses x18 register as a shadow stack pointer that attackers cannot corrupt through normal stack overflow. This is the strongest single protection against ROP chains on this architecture.

UNMAP_KERNEL_AT_EL0 is the ARM64 equivalent of KPTI — unmaps kernel pages when running in userspace, closing the Meltdown side channel completely.

INIT_ON_ALLOC and INIT_ON_FREE zero memory on every allocation and free — eliminates uninitialized memory reads and prevents use-after-free information leaks from stale heap data.

